ith the land and are often  portrayed as having a deep connection to  it the fair Focus seen as a  representation of the mysterious and  unknown forces of nature and the power  of the imagination Organa being the  leader of the fairies is particularly  fitting if we consider that her epithet  lafaye actually means the fairy however  something worth considering here is that  this epithet wasn't introduced until  many centuries after morgana's  introduction in literature in fact the  first writer to refer to Morgana as  Morgana lafaye was Thomas Mallory in one  of his works from the 15th century in  some versions of Legends Morgana is  portrayed as a villain who seeks to harm  or kill King Arthur while in other she  is a more complex character with  motivations that are not entirely evil  this aspect of her character is entirely  dependent on Whose accounts we're going  by Morgana lafaye's character has  appeared in many works of literature  including the medieval poem Le Mort de  Artur Mallory's work modern novel The  myths of Avalon and first and foremost  Jeffrey of monmouth's work Vita merlini  or the life of Merlin which was written  in 1150 Visa merlini was a Latin poem  which told the story of Merlin's Madness  his life as a wild man of the woods and  his prophecies and conversations with  his sister in many different Works  Morgana satisfies the role of powerful  sorceress and chief antagonist known for  her beauty and her ability to use magic  to seduce men she is also known for her  enmity towards Merlin and her desire to  kill him usually acting as the main  rival of Merlin and sometimes the one  that is responsible for his death these  texts present Morgana as a powerful and  cunning wedge who uses her beauty and  her magical powers to manipulate and  deceive others within Vita merlini  Morgana is referred to as Morgan a name  which means Seaborn the name survived in  Middle Welsh as morian and the cognate  form in Old Irish is muigen the name of  a shape-