rd describes her as a very  powerful wedge I think that it's  reasonable to assume that Morgana was  extremely versed in the dark arts  possessing knowledge of all of the dark  spells that we are accustomed to and  perhaps many more if she was the  adversary of Merlin the most powerful  wizard to have ever lived I imagine she  must have had a few tricks up her sleeve  in Arthurian Legend Morgana is said to  possess a wide range of magical  abilities she is known to be skilled in  the art of healing and is often depicted  as a powerful herbalist and healer  typically healing and the ability to  heal are paired with individuals  associated with moral goodness or  righteousness and so I felt it  noteworthy to mention that Morgana  entirely contradicts this  she is also known to possess the ability  to shapeshift and is said to be able to  take on the form of animals birds and  other creatures from the sounds of it  Morgana was probably one of the first if  not the first animagus that is a Witcher  wizard that is able to transform into an  animal at will however the noteworthy  exception here is that Morgana was able  to transform into a multitude of  creatures not just one a testament to  her exceptional magical ability  additionally she is said to have been  able to control the elements possessing  the power to summon storms and control  the winds Elemental Magic is very much  prevalent in Harry Potter but for the  most part appears to be reserved for the  most powerful witches and wizards people  like Voldemort and Dumbledore the best  example of Elemental Magic on display in  totality was during Voldemort and  Dumbledore's duel inside the ministry  Atrium she is also known to be able to  teleport and transport herself and  others over long distances did that  sound like an ability in Harry Potter to  you that's right Morgana knew Apparition  but the vast list of magical abilities  that Morgana possessed that have been  boasted about by copious pieces of  literature 